TI  - Relation Detection to Identify Stroke Assertions from Clinical Notes Using 
      Natural Language Processing.
PG  - 619-623
LID - 10.3233/SHTI231039 [doi]
AB  - According to the World Stroke Organization, 12.2 million people world-wide will 
      have their first stroke this year almost half of which will die as a result. 
      Natural Language Processing (NLP) may improve stroke phenotyping; however, 
      existing rule-based classifiers are rigid, resulting in inadequate performance. 
      We report findings from a pilot study using NLP to improve relation detection for 
      stroke assertion detection to support research studies and healthcare operations.
