DP  - 2022 Feb
TI  - Automated information extraction from free-text medical documents for stroke key 
      performance indicators: a pilot study.
PG  - 315-317
LID - 10.1111/imj.15678 [doi]
AB  - Automated information extraction might be able to assist with the collection of 
      stroke key performance indicators (KPI). The feasibility of using natural 
      language processing for classification-based KPI and datetime field extraction 
      was assessed. Using free-text discharge summaries, random forest models achieved 
      high levels of performance in classification tasks (area under the receiver 
      operator curve 0.95-1.00). The datetime field extraction method was successful in 
      29 of 43 (67.4%) cases. Further studies are indicated.
